    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Near Place du Pin and the harbour district, Babbo Mio serves Italian cuisine in one of Nice's lively neighbourhoods, with a large sunny terrace.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The current listing of the official Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office (explorenicecotedazur.com) now states, consistently in its French and English versions, that pets are not accepted. We follow this version rather than an older positive confirmation found in an earlier search, which probably reflected a previous version of the listing. The restaurant's own website (babbomio.com) says nothing either way about pets.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: according to the official tourist office, dogs are not accepted here. Plan another address with your dog, or call to check if you want to be sure.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Place Garibaldi and the harbour of Nice are just steps away, for a walk with your dog.</p>
